# Selected first Gamma public owner - source proposal only

This package adds a public construction-associated owner around the held
`rust-gamma-prep-02` pure Gamma function. It is unapplied, unformatted and
unexecuted. Root and another author must read the complete source before any
future application or execution. No gate or numerical PASS is claimed.

The public API is
`initialize_construction_ctf_first_gammas(&ConstructionCtfFirstAssembly,
&ConstructionCtfFirstMatrixFunctions) -> ConstructionCtfFirstGammas`.
It borrows the actual ordered exponential/inverse return from the existing
combined first-method API. It does not invoke either prerequisite API.

The wrapper requires the actual original construction ID, first assembly
ordinal one, selected one-dimensional/no-source route and reset selectors.
It checks predecessor IDs, dimensions and all actual context fields; both
floating-point context fields are compared by bits, preserving signed zero
and any unchanged NaN payload. No caller timestep is inferred from histories,
and no equality between caller timestep and current CTF timestep is imposed.

One successful call passes actual inverse AInv, exponential AExp, original
assembly IdenMatrix/BMat and unchanged current context to the pure Gamma API.
It copies no substitute identity or default arrays. It does not reconstruct
AMat, exponential, inverse, B, timestep, route or retry state. It introduces
no finite, conditioning or zero-duration arithmetic guard.

Prerequisite assembly/exponential stops, actual inverse non-invocation and
invoked-inverse errors remain distinct typed unavailable results with no
Gamma arrays. Association, unsupported context and shape errors are also
explicit. A successful result retains the actual pure Gamma observation,
including ATemp, Gamma1 and Gamma2, not final coefficient or whole-call state.

The existing ordered predecessor API establishes the actual06 then05 calls;
this proposal adds one07 call only when its supplied returns are available.
Public Rust structs remain caller-owned: identity/context checks do not prove
that arbitrarily forged structs came from a particular execution. Future
production wiring must pass the genuine same-owner return without mutation.

Only `heat_balance/mod.rs` receives a declaration-only proposed change.
Its current canonical bytes are separately archived. The Gamma pure module
and its separate `surface_manager.rs` declaration proposal remain immutable
in held `rust-gamma-prep-02`; they are dependencies, not recopied changes.
The public05/06/combined modules are still held prospective dependencies.
Future composition must preserve their reviewed declarations and refresh
the current parent before applying; this package does not install them.

Six source-focused routing tests are authored, not run: actual borrowed
prerequisite immutability and output ownership, all source unavailable
routes, distinct predecessor errors/non-invocation, construction/ordinal and
signed-zero context mismatch, unsupported source/perpendicular context,
and unrepaired predecessor dimensions/buffer shape. Their positive fixture
calls actual Rust assembly and existing combined predecessor APIs on literal
test inputs. Negative tests mutate typed input owners deliberately. They use
no Native answers or production fixtures and do not certify source formulas.

No cache/state/driver activation, retry loop, Native source/artifact, operand
file, observer, policy, tolerance, QA framework or execution stage is added.
No project/target import, compile, formatter, test, engine or binary/weather/
scientific result read was performed. Canonical files and Git are untouched.
The author also authored earlier Native/helper/ingress source, so independent
peer acceptance is source/protocol review, not self-formula certification.
